{"created": "2026-11-05T18:04:13.146785+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-05T18:04:13.402545+00:00", "id": 23986406, "conceptrecid": "22986529", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23986406", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22986529", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23986406", "metadata": {"title": "One Object, Three Descriptions: Axes, Images and Grids of a Jacquard Pattern System", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23986406", "publication_date": "2026-11-05", "description": "<p class=\"FirstParagraph\"><span>Version 1.4.0 (v10) of &ldquo;One Object, Three Descriptions&rdquo;. The paper shows that three separate descriptions of a Jacquard pattern system present one finite structure: sixteen families of axes combined by a parity rule, sixty three-tint images with 512 grids, and the level sets of a square-plate eigenmode.</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\"><span>The historical theorems are kept. New Sections 10 and 11 connect the description to: - the balanced ansate-cross sources and their strata; - the graphical equivalences between them; - the 62 selected classes and their 52 radial spectral signatures.</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\"><span>Version 1.2.1 is kept in historique-v1.2.1/. The spectral counts are finite results at period twelve.</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\"><span>Licence: texts and figures under CC BY 4.0; code under AGPL v3.</span></p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Amiot, Anibal Edelberto", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0002-6414-9448"}], "keywords": ["Jacquard weaving", "parity figures", "linear codes", "level sets", "square plate eigenmodes", "Chladni figures", "half-shift criterion", "doubling map", "arithmogeometry"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22965031", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22862110", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.22866061", "relati